 // Reject targets where privileged instructions are obviously unavailable.
 // TODO: Some embedded OSes should probably be accepted here.
+// BlueOS ESP32-C3 provides pointer-width atomics through __atomic* calls,
+// despite lacking hardware atomics. With target_os="blueos", this triggers
+// the OS check below. BlueOS RISC-V kernel code runs in M-mode and can
+// disable interrupts, so allow its privileged fallbacks. The selected
+// feature's safety requirements still apply.
+#[cfg(not(all(target_os = "blueos", target_arch = "riscv32")))]
 #[cfg(any(portable_atomic_unsafe_assume_single_core, portable_atomic_unsafe_assume_privileged))]
 #[cfg(any(
     target_arch = "arm",
     target_arch = "avr",
